  "term": "Paris Medical School",
  "definition": "Paris Medical School refers to the Université de Paris medical school in Paris, France, formed from the recent merger of the Paris Nord and Paris Centre sites. In the source, it is described as one of the largest medical schools in France and as the setting for a large-scale objective structured clinical examination for fourth-year medical students.",
